WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.040
Hello, champ! Ready for Chapter 4?

2
00:00:08.040 --> 00:00:18.360
Ch 1: Computers · Ch 2: Binary · Ch 3: Devices

3
00:00:18.360 --> 00:00:23.260
Chapter 4 · How Websites Talk to Each Other

4
00:00:23.260 --> 00:00:30.350
Say with me: Websites talk to each other!

5
00:00:30.350 --> 00:00:36.690
The secret trip of a website

6
00:00:36.690 --> 00:00:42.450
Where does the cartoon come from?

7
00:00:42.450 --> 00:00:50.050
Is it hiding inside your tablet? Think!

8
00:00:50.050 --> 00:01:01.840
It comes from another computer, far away!

9
00:01:01.840 --> 00:01:14.010
Internet = millions of computers joined together

10
00:01:14.010 --> 00:01:23.300
ASKERS: your tablet, phone, laptop

11
00:01:23.300 --> 00:01:33.720
ANSWERERS: servers keep websites ready

12
00:01:33.720 --> 00:01:40.230
Internet = asking and answering

13
00:01:40.230 --> 00:01:45.270
Say: Ask… and answer!

14
00:01:45.270 --> 00:01:52.330
A website is like a shop

15
00:01:52.330 --> 00:02:00.300
Your home has an address

16
00:02:00.300 --> 00:02:09.950
A website's address = URL

17
00:02:09.950 --> 00:02:19.580
mentr.com → the name + the ending

18
00:02:19.580 --> 00:02:27.770
Say: URL = website address

19
00:02:27.770 --> 00:02:36.940
Questions travel on invisible roads

20
00:02:36.940 --> 00:02:44.820
Wi-Fi: a road from the router

21
00:02:44.820 --> 00:02:53.560
Mobile data: a road through towers

22
00:02:53.560 --> 00:03:01.820
Roads only CARRY questions and answers

23
00:03:01.820 --> 00:03:06.530
Follow one trip, step by step

24
00:03:06.530 --> 00:03:13.130
Step 1: You type the address

25
00:03:13.130 --> 00:03:22.950
Step 2: Your device asks — a request

26
00:03:22.950 --> 00:03:28.620
Step 3: The server finds the page

27
00:03:28.620 --> 00:03:35.340
Step 4: The server sends it back

28
00:03:35.340 --> 00:03:41.510
Step 5: The page appears!

29
00:03:41.510 --> 00:03:48.140
All in less than 1 second!

30
00:03:48.140 --> 00:03:54.220
Game: fix the mixed-up steps

31
00:03:54.220 --> 00:04:09.180
Put them in order — think!

32
00:04:09.180 --> 00:04:20.660
Type address → Device asks → Page appears

33
00:04:20.660 --> 00:04:27.000
Watching a cartoon online

34
00:04:27.000 --> 00:04:37.370
Ask for the next piece… answer… again!

35
00:04:37.370 --> 00:04:46.970
Slow road → spinning circle (buffering)

36
00:04:46.970 --> 00:04:52.450
Practice check

37
00:04:52.450 --> 00:05:02.730
First: page appears, or device asks?

38
00:05:02.730 --> 00:05:09.100
Hint: can a server answer before you ask?

39
00:05:09.100 --> 00:05:16.540
Answer: your device ASKS first

40
00:05:16.540 --> 00:05:23.740
Internet = computers asking & answering

41
00:05:23.740 --> 00:05:29.500
Website = shop · Address = URL

42
00:05:29.500 --> 00:05:35.380
Wi-Fi & mobile data = roads

43
00:05:35.380 --> 00:05:41.820
Type → Ask → Page appears

44
00:05:41.820 --> 00:05:50.390
Chapter 4 complete!

45
00:05:50.390 --> 00:05:59.490
Next: Quiz · Tap Finish
